# Kaijudo Game UI Design System

## Project Overview
Kaijudo is a digital card game based on Duel Masters TCG rules. This is an Nx monorepo with React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS 4, Tauri (desktop), Convex (backend), and Clerk (auth).

## Design Aesthetic
Premium fantasy TCG client inspired by WarcraftCN (https://www.warcraftcn.com/) component techniques but with a Duel Masters / Japanese anime aesthetic. NOT a WarcraftCN clone — we use their CSS techniques (border-image frames, glow effects, textured backgrounds) adapted to our civilization color system.

## Civilization Color Tokens
- Light (Gold): #FFD700 primary, #FFF8DC glow
- Water (Blue): #1E90FF primary, #87CEEB glow
- Darkness (Purple): #8B00FF primary, #DDA0DD glow
- Fire (Red): #FF4500 primary, #FF6347 glow
- Nature (Green): #32CD32 primary, #90EE90 glow
- Neutral UI: #1a1a2e bg, #16213e panels, #e0e0e0 text

## Key Conventions
- Dark-first design — all components assume dark backgrounds
- Use Tailwind CSS 4 (NOT inline styles)
- Use Motion library for animations (200-400ms interactions, up to 800ms dramatic)
- Use Radix UI for accessible primitives
- Components go in packages/ (monorepo), not directly in apps/
- Always accept `civilization` prop for themed components
- Support size variants: sm, md, lg
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion

## Game Architecture
- `packages/game-engine/` — Pure TypeScript game logic, no React
- `packages/react-game-ui/` — Battlefield components, zone displays, indicators
- `packages/react-game-types/` — Shared types (Civilization, Rarity, Race, Creature)
- `packages/react-card/` — Card component with 3D tilt and holographic effects

## Duel Masters Game Rules (for context)
- 40-card deck, 5 shields, 5-card opening hand
- Zones: Hand, Battle Zone, Mana Zone, Shield Zone, Graveyard, Deck
- Turn: Untap → Draw → Charge Mana → Summon/Cast → Attack
- Summoning sickness on creatures
- Win: break all shields + direct attack, or opponent decks out
